<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:11:04 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Big EU defence projects under threat from proposed budget cuts: Commissioner Andrius Kubilius</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261127-big-eu-defence-projects-under-threat-from-proposed-budget-cuts-commissioner-andrius-kubilius</link><description>
We speak to the EU's Commissioner for Defence and Space, Andrius Kubilius. The former prime minister of Lithuania – who grew up during the Soviet era – tells us how he sees the confrontation between Europe and Russia. He also sounds the alarm over proposed cuts in the EU's future budget, saying that they could jeopardise major European projects in defence and space. Kubilius praises the EU's SAFE defence loans programme, remarking that it has been "really very successful".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8b20618-ea78-11f1-9216-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-ANDRIUS-KUBILIUS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8b20618-ea78-11f1-9216-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-ANDRIUS-KUBILIUS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">49820856-e755-11f1-84a1-434b5653c453</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:03:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>From cyberbullying to extremist content, can EU Kids Act protect minors online?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261127-from-cyberbullying-to-extremist-content-can-eu-kids-act-protect-minors-online</link><description>
Almost every European teenager is online. Some 96 percent of 15-year-olds use social media, yet many say they do not feel safe there. One in four children in the EU, aged 12 to 17, report having experienced cyberbullying, and nearly one in three say social media has left them feeling stressed, sad or socially excluded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce32d74e-e7fd-11f1-a05d-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/MONTAGE-DEBAT-EU-KIDS-ACT-EN.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce32d74e-e7fd-11f1-a05d-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/MONTAGE-DEBAT-EU-KIDS-ACT-EN.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0eeb14a4-e754-11f1-8221-e7c8c9070cee</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:02:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jennifer BEN BRAHIM</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>With Spain’s far right on the cusp of power, can women bail Sanchez out once again?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261127-spain-far-right-vox-at-the-gates-can-women-bail-out-sanchez-once-again</link><description>
Spanish women’s refusal to surrender hard-won rights helped Socialist Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez clinch an unlikely victory in a snap election three years ago. As he gambles with another early vote on Sunday, his hopes of defying the odds rest on women again rallying to block the far right from governing Spain for the first time since Francisco Franco’s dictatorship.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7579c0a2-ea75-11f1-ac9d-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316749506716.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7579c0a2-ea75-11f1-ac9d-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316749506716.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba77f322-ea70-11f1-81bf-0955ae07043a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:27:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7579c0a2-ea75-11f1-ac9d-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316749506716.jpg">© Rocio Ruz, Europa Press via AP</source><dc:creator>Benjamin DODMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Spanish PM Sanchez makes final campaign push to beat the right ahead of crunch vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261127-sanchez-makes-last-bid-to-beat-the-right-ahead-of-spanish-vote</link><description>
Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez makes his final campaign push with a rally in Madrid Friday, the last day of campaigning for Sunday's high-stakes elections. Opinion polls show the Socialist premier lagging behind the main right-wing Popular Party (PP) as the Spanish vote opens an electoral cycle over the next 12 months that could reshape the balance of power within the EU. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f8aa164-ea51-11f1-a0d5-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/8fc348c708cdc4651d7877edc47076fb001aea55.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f8aa164-ea51-11f1-a0d5-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/8fc348c708cdc4651d7877edc47076fb001aea55.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">503949a8-ea51-11f1-a79e-edb6ba993705</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:57:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f8aa164-ea51-11f1-a0d5-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/8fc348c708cdc4651d7877edc47076fb001aea55.jpg">© Josep Lago, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Trump calls on Putin to end all 'military aggression' against Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261127-live-trump-calls-on-putin-to-end-all-military-aggression-against-europe</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said on Thursday that he had urged his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin to "pull back all military aggression against territories throughout Europe". Although Trump did not provide any further details, he added that he hoped this would pave the way for a peace deal to be struck between Kyiv and Moscow. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/630aef0e-ea2f-11f1-99a9-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-26T162433Z-1015617438-RC2TQOANQQ5V-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-TRUMP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/630aef0e-ea2f-11f1-99a9-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-26T162433Z-1015617438-RC2TQOANQQ5V-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-TRUMP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e883771e-ea48-11f1-b857-4993d8739c5d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:22:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/630aef0e-ea2f-11f1-99a9-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-26T162433Z-1015617438-RC2TQOANQQ5V-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-TRUMP.jpg">© Vyacheslav Prokofyev, Sputnik via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>France and Germany push for EU budget deal by year-end as far-right rise threatens Ukraine aid</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261127-france-and-germany-push-for-eu-budget-deal-by-year-end-as-far-right-rise-threatens-ukraine-aid</link><description>
As Europe braces itself for a slew of tense elections in 2027, Paris and Berlin are pushing for the European Union to strike a budget deal by December 31 to lock in financial aid for Ukraine. But Thursday's talks in Brussels seem to have done little to build consensus around the bloc's next budget.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc7e33b4-ea20-11f1-92cc-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-26T195141Z-1710060570-RC2VVOA3Q7FW-RTRMADP-3-EU-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc7e33b4-ea20-11f1-92cc-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-26T195141Z-1710060570-RC2VVOA3Q7FW-RTRMADP-3-EU-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0bfb95b2-ea37-11f1-a8be-cd02365843b6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:17:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc7e33b4-ea20-11f1-92cc-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-26T195141Z-1710060570-RC2VVOA3Q7FW-RTRMADP-3-EU-SUMMIT.jpg">© Stephanie Lecocq, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Is Spain's snap election being rigged? Debunking viral claims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261126-is-spain-s-snap-election-being-rigged-debunking-viral-claims</link><description>
Ahead of Spain's snap election on Sunday, allegations of vote rigging – known in Spanish as "pucherazo" – are spreading widely on social media. From claims that undocumented migrants are being illegally registered to vote, to allegations that postal ballots and vote counts could be manipulated, internet users are accusing Pedro Sanchez's government of attempting to rig the election. But these claims misrepresent how Spain's electoral system works, as Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77702156-e9e6-11f1-a3f6-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-11-26-231045.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77702156-e9e6-11f1-a3f6-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/Screenshot-2026-11-26-231045.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e214e08-e9e7-11f1-8dc7-df74d954d1c7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:17:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>'Citizens angry with the establishment' as Spain heads to the polls</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261126-citizens-angry-with-the-establishment-as-spain-heads-to-the-polls</link><description>
Three party leaders are vying in Spain's general election on Sunday, which leftist Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez called following a parliamentary setback over housing legislation that underscored the fragility of his minority coalition government.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f7dcd80-ea59-11f1-bbfd-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1931a9c1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f7dcd80-ea59-11f1-bbfd-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1931a9c1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1419df4c-e9e7-11f1-ae5b-7fa173d8c7de</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:16:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Citizens angry with the establishment' as Spain heads to the polls</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/citizens-angry-with-the-establishment-as-spain-heads-to-the-polls</link><description>
Three party leaders are vying in Spain's general election on Sunday, which leftist Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez called following a parliamentary setback over housing legislation that underscored the fragility of his minority coalition government.
 
Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Javier Carbonell, Policy Analyst at the European Policy Centre, says that despite solid economic growth in Spain the population "have suffered a housing crisis and inflation, citizens are still angry with the government and the economic system regardless of macroeconomic data", adding that "in the end citizens are angry with the establishment, in this case it will be Sanchez, but to be honest I think they will be angry at PP and Vox very soon".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f7dcd80-ea59-11f1-bbfd-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1931a9c1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f7dcd80-ea59-11f1-bbfd-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1931a9c1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">068bd566-e9e6-11f1-9a78-fd75ce30ac41</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:15:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Sanchez's big gamble: Will Spain swing from Socialists to hard right?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261126-sanchez-s-big-gamble-will-spain-swing-from-socialists-to-hard-right</link><description>
For eight years, he’s been a mainstay among European leaders, one who’s snatched victory from the jaws of defeat before. But has Pedro Sanchez run out of road this time? Spain's Socialist prime minister is dogged by incumbent fatigue and nepotism allegations. By calling a snap general election, Sanchez is gambling on turning the rift in his coalition over his country's housing shortage into a referendum on his country's strong growth.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd2c626e-e9cb-11f1-a182-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T191001Z-29917429-RC27VOA4BVBZ-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-ELECTION-PP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd2c626e-e9cb-11f1-a182-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T191001Z-29917429-RC27VOA4BVBZ-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-ELECTION-PP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7d701670-e9c7-11f1-bdb1-23595fa0119e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:53:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump urges Putin to end 'military aggression' in Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-urges-putin-to-end-military-aggression-in-europe</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said Thursday he had asked Vladimir Putin to "pull back all military aggression" against Europe, in a shift in tone towards the leader Russian he called his friend just a week ago. Trump said he had made the request to Putin when they met in China last week, adding that he thought it would help lead to a deal to end Moscow's grinding war in Ukraine. The US leader's comments come a day after he hosted NATO chief Mark Rutte in Florida, after which they issued a joint statement calling on Russia not to expand the Ukraine war. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6c3707a-e9d4-11f1-8cb6-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-200333-200843-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6c3707a-e9d4-11f1-8cb6-174dac1c1bf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-200333-200843-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dbdd4d2e-e9d4-11f1-8be7-516fc2299180</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:10:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Le Pen slams push for EU budget deal before French election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/le-pen-slams-push-for-eu-budget-deal-before-french-election</link><description>
EU leaders locked horns over the bloc's budget at a summit meeting in Brussels on Thursday, as far-right leader Marine Le Pen slammed an "underhanded" push to lock in the long-term spending plans before French presidential elections next year. European Council head Antonio Costa turned up the pressure upon arrival at the budget talks, where heavyweight Germany is pressing for cuts as well as burden-sharing on money for Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2c2241c-e9d2-11f1-a270-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-200845-201341-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2c2241c-e9d2-11f1-a270-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-200845-201341-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a7a2cb26-e9d2-11f1-83e2-f598b54f400c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:02:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Will Spain's far right replace Europe's left-wing stalwart?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-will-spain-s-far-right-replace-europe-s-left-wing-stalwart</link><description>
Some 39 million Spaniards will head to the ballot this Sunday to vote in early general elections. Latest polls put the conservative Popular Party ahead of incumbent PM Pedro Sanchez’s Socialists. The third-strongest political force, however, is the far-right Vox party. A strong showing at Sunday’s election could see them form Spain’s next government. FRANCE 24 explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13ac116c-e9b8-11f1-b82e-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-Spain-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13ac116c-e9b8-11f1-b82e-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-Spain-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34c2cfb2-e9b8-11f1-bd33-01df7f3018c8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:51:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Spanish economist de Cos to succeed Lagarde as head of ECB</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-spanish-economist-de-cos-succeed-lagarde-head-ecb</link><description>
Spanish monetary economist Pablo Hernandez de Cos on Thursday was set to replace France's Christine Lagarde as the new head of the European Central Bank (ECB). His nomination comes as the Europe's most powerful financial institution grapples with an Iran war-driven resurgence in inflation and a cost of living crisis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8782840e-e9a4-11f1-a5e6-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25290616236227.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8782840e-e9a4-11f1-a5e6-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25290616236227.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c00b4f90-e9a9-11f1-b052-5576e34b99b1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:55:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8782840e-e9a4-11f1-a5e6-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25290616236227.jpg">© Jose Luis Magana, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>How far-right Vox is winning over young voters ahead of Spain's snap election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-how-far-right-vox-winning-over-young-voters-ahead-spain-snap-election</link><description>
Spain's Vox party is winning over many young people ahead of the country's snap election on November 29, particularly men. The far-right party is capitalising on the rising cost of living and anti-immigrant sentiment to expand its once-marginal electoral base. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/714af09c-e8ee-11f1-9f73-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4QF6P2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/714af09c-e8ee-11f1-9f73-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4QF6P2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0269e4aa-e9a0-11f1-97de-138fc9f0a0ac</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:37:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/714af09c-e8ee-11f1-9f73-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4QF6P2.jpg">© Cesar Manso, AFP</source><dc:creator>Barbara GABEL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Housing crisis on the ballot: Anger boils over ahead of Spanish election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261126-housing-crisis-on-the-ballot-anger-boils-over-ahead-of-spanish-election</link><description>
Spaniards head to the polls on Sunday in a general election that was called after street protests for affordable housing. Anger bubbled over after 87-year-old Maricarmen Abascal was evicted from her home of seven decades and two decrees to tackle the housing crisis were rejected by parliament. In calling the snap election, Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez is hoping the housing issue can galvanise his left-wing base.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fad2a10-e99c-11f1-be69-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a49da062.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fad2a10-e99c-11f1-be69-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a49da062.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e0a5da54-e8fa-11f1-bd51-89765fe8c5bf</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:33:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Maude Petit-Jové</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA['Europe has two kinds of countries: Small countries & those that haven’t yet realised they’re small’]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe-has-two-kinds-of-countries-small-countries-those-that-haven-t-yet-realised-they-re-small</link><description>
“The implications of having the far right in power in Brussels are enormous,” warns Sophie Pornschlegel, Senior Advisor at the European Policy Centre. With elections approaching in several EU member states, including France and Italy, what would a growing number of far-right, Eurosceptic governments mean for the EU budget, relations between European institutions, common legislation and support for Ukraine? Could Giorgia Meloni could adopt a more radical stance? “The whole idea of the EU is to have a common legislation that is then applied in 27 member states. Otherwise, what is the point of having the EU?”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa874ada-e994-11f1-97fb-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-080650-081732-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa874ada-e994-11f1-97fb-77d069279b82/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261126-080650-081732-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0002fdce-e995-11f1-9cb2-21ab8fbc63ca</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:31:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU leaders face showdown over Ukraine funding as divisions deepen</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-eu-leaders-face-showdown-over-ukraine-funding-as-divisions-deepen</link><description>
European Union leaders on Thursday are set to tackle deep divisions as they meet in Brussels to discuss the bloc's long-term budget in Brussels, which includes a proposed €45 billion loan to keep Ukraine funded through 2027. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/981f9684-e43c-11f1-b116-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/union-europeenne.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/981f9684-e43c-11f1-b116-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/union-europeenne.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c93d6544-e963-11f1-80e0-0b530df5f565</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 06:56:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/981f9684-e43c-11f1-b116-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/union-europeenne.jpeg">© Yves Herman, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine has ‘no intention’ of extending war to Libya, FM says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261126-live-eu-leaders-face-showdown-over-ukraine-funding-as-divisions-deepen</link><description>
Ukraine was not attempting to spread the war with Russia to Libyan shores by attacking two Russian ships off the coast of Benghazi, Kyiv's Foreign Minister Andriy Sybiga said Thursday, shortly after a phone call with his Libyan counterpart. The attack in the Mediterranean has sparked fears that the war was expanding beyond European front lines. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/856ab7e2-e754-11f1-8168-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26327310217136.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/856ab7e2-e754-11f1-8168-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26327310217136.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e21235e-e949-11f1-968f-a7bfed69f39a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:44:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/856ab7e2-e754-11f1-8168-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26327310217136.jpg">© AP via Security Service of Ukraine</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU says 'strongly' rejects premise of new US tariffs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/eu-says-strongly-rejects-premise-of-new-us-tariffs</link><description>
The EU said Wednesday that it rejected the premise of new tariffs on its exports proposed by the United States and expected Washington to stick by a deal struck with Brussels last year. The US unveiled proposed tariffs on 14 economies including the European Union and China, after a months-long probe into alleged excess production. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d88720f4-e908-11f1-ab85-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-203356-203840-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d88720f4-e908-11f1-ab85-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-203356-203840-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ddbab02c-e908-11f1-8992-01a3940a6265</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:48:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Poland says will create no-fly zone at Ukraine border after repeated airspace violations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/poland-says-will-create-no-fly-zone-at-ukraine-border-after-repeated-airspace-violations</link><description>
Poland will soon create a no-fly zone near the Ukrainian border, a deputy defence minister announced on Wednesday, after several incursions into its airspace it blamed on Russia. Poland backs Ukraine as it fights off Russia's near five-year invasion and has repeatedly accused Moscow of seeking to target Kyiv's supporters with drone incursions and other methods. The no-fly zone is intended to allow Polish forces to quickly identify any Russian military aircraft and shoot them down if necessary. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/008c6c02-e905-11f1-b02d-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-200844-201037-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/008c6c02-e905-11f1-b02d-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261125-200844-201037-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06520944-e905-11f1-9844-d78cece7454c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:22:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Turkey's deadly factory blast: 'Investing in safety costs more than letting people die'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-factory-blast-turkey-izmir</link><description>
An explosion at a steel factory on November 9 in Turkey's Aliaga, near Izmir, killed 19 people. This tragedy follows several others and highlights the issues surrounding workers’ safety in Turkey, our Observers say. They also condemn the repressive responses from the government and the company.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a9c570a-e4f0-11f1-8fbd-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-pic-3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a9c570a-e4f0-11f1-8fbd-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-pic-3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e7bc4040-e4f3-11f1-baf7-bf9bfc08e1ba</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:28:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a9c570a-e4f0-11f1-8fbd-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-pic-3.jpg">© The Observers</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Moldova launches national preparedness campaign after drone incursions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/moldova-launches-national-preparedness-campaign-after-drone-incursions</link><description>
Moldova is urging its citizens to prepare for emergencies as the war in neighbouring Ukraine brings new risks across its border. The “Moldova Ready” campaign, launched in Chisinau, includes a display of the remains of a drone carrying 52kg of explosives after it crashed in the country last month. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b6c9bac8-e8ed-11f1-b140-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261124-233651-233836-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b6c9bac8-e8ed-11f1-b140-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261124-233651-233836-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bbd2ac6e-e8ed-11f1-8613-cb8a77ed3465</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:34:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Kremlin declines comment on reports 700,000 Russian soldiers killed in Ukraine war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-kremlin-declines-comment-reports-700-000-russian-soldiers-killed-ukraine-war</link><description>
Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov on Wednesday declined to comment on reports in Russian and international news outlets that around 700,000 Russian soldiers have been killed in the Ukraine war so far. The reports were based on hacked data from Russia's official statistics agency. Peskov said only the defence ministry can disclose figures and told reporters "not to pay attention to any other data".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/537505cc-e8de-11f1-8609-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26308532895133.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/537505cc-e8de-11f1-8609-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26308532895133.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b3a52b8e-e8de-11f1-ab22-97c75752944e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:14:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/537505cc-e8de-11f1-8609-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26308532895133.jpg">© Dmitri Lovetsky, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Surprise Eurostar strike cancels London, Paris and Brussels trains</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-surprise-eurostar-strike-cancels-london-paris-and-brussels-trains</link><description>
Several Eurostar trains connecting London, Paris and Brussels were cancelled in a surprise strike on Wednesday. The train operator did not specify who exactly was striking or the reasons why.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5292c004-e8b6-11f1-b877-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6LZ3KE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5292c004-e8b6-11f1-b877-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6LZ3KE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">258eda56-e8b7-11f1-aa87-334f30cc40c2</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:02:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5292c004-e8b6-11f1-b877-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6LZ3KE.jpg">© Sameer Al-Doumy, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Two Libyan soldiers killed in Ukrainian attack on Russian vessels in Benghazi</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-live-two-libyan-soldiers-killed-in-ukrainian-attack-on-russian-vessels-in-benghazi</link><description>
Two Libyan soldiers have died from wounds sustained in an attack, claimed by Ukraine, on Russian ships near Benghazi, a senior figure in the administration in eastern Libya said late on Tuesday. Members of the European Parliament will convene in Strasbourg Wednesday to discuss "Europe’s role and capacity to protect the international order and secure a just and lasting peace for Ukraine". Read our live blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd313f6c-e76f-11f1-85b8-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T102302Z-464352545-RC2MTOAS4A1W-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd313f6c-e76f-11f1-85b8-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T102302Z-464352545-RC2MTOAS4A1W-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9cb769e-e882-11f1-bedd-f5a26d42d6d4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:46:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd313f6c-e76f-11f1-85b8-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-23T102302Z-464352545-RC2MTOAS4A1W-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS.jpg">© Volodymyr Zelenskiy via Telegram, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine seeks €115 billion in foreign aid for 2027, Zelensky says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-ukraine-seeks-%E2%82%AC115-billion-in-foreign-aid-for-2027-zelensky-says</link><description>
Ukraine will need €115 billion in external financing next year to sustain its economy and war effort against Russia, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Tuesday, adding that Kyiv had secured commitments for about €90 billion from the European Union.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c5b81ec4-d3af-11f1-94da-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T085801Z-1180937654-RC284OA1JXI9-RTRMADP-3-EU-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c5b81ec4-d3af-11f1-94da-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T085801Z-1180937654-RC284OA1JXI9-RTRMADP-3-EU-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4487faee-e86e-11f1-ac0a-ffe9b02711fe</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:19:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c5b81ec4-d3af-11f1-94da-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-16T085801Z-1180937654-RC284OA1JXI9-RTRMADP-3-EU-SUMMIT.jpg">© Stéphanie Lecocq, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russian nuclear satellites plan 'foolhardy', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russian-nuclear-satellites-plan-foolhardy-expert-says</link><description>
NATO chief Mark Rutte said Monday the alliance would defend against threats in space when asked about German media reports that Russia may be preparing to launch a nuclear-armed satellite. Speaking to FRANCE 24, Dafydd Townley, Senior Teaching Fellow in International Security at the University of Portsmouth, says that the alleged plan would be "foolhardy because the impact would be indiscriminate, they wouldn't be able to choose only Western or non-Russian satellites".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ab32d036-e844-11f1-af20-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261124-210517-211328-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ab32d036-e844-11f1-af20-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261124-210517-211328-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b020b4d2-e844-11f1-ad62-4df93936b03d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:31:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russian losses on Ukrainian front top 700,000 including missing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russian-losses-on-ukrainian-front-top-700-000-including-missing</link><description>
New analysis of leaked Russian government data suggests more than 700,000 Russian soldiers have died in the war against Ukraine. Independent Russian media outlets have updated their estimates of Moscow's military casualties, including soldiers missing on the frontline, after Belarusian and Ukrainian hackers obtained figures from the Russian statistics agency. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f196246a-e83a-11f1-93dd-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261124-200144-200306-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f196246a-e83a-11f1-93dd-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261124-200144-200306-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6f2d1a6-e83a-11f1-beca-d5e1509a4784</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:22:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia's war on Ukraine: 'Both sides are prepared to operate outside of the conflict zone'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-both-sides-are-prepared-to-operate-outside-of-the-conflict-zone</link><description>
Charli James is pleased to welcome Gavin Hall, Teaching Fellow in Political Science, and International Security at the University of Strathclyde. Hall examines recent Russian and Ukrainian operations beyond the main conflict zone, the conditions necessary for a negotiated settlement and the implications of diminishing direct US military support for Ukraine. “Both sides are prepared to operate beyond the main battleground and outside of the conflict zone,” he explains. Hall discusses why both sides want to negotiate from a position of strength and the conditions under which a “mutually hurting stalemate” could lead to a negotiated settlement. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7262fe1c-e820-11f1-9829-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261124-130504-131126-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7262fe1c-e820-11f1-9829-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261124-130504-131126-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">780f43fc-e820-11f1-bf9a-37dddb6a2e55</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:26:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
